, /w/images/2/26/Gold_Icon.png 1.5x\"><img alt=\"Price: 500 gp\" src=\"/w/images/thumb/2/26/Gold_Icon.png/25px-Gold_Icon.png.webp\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"25\" height=\"25\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></picture></span><a href=\"/w/images/2/26/Gold_Icon.png\" class=\"mw-file-source\" title=\"View source image\"><!-- Image link for Crawlers --></a></span></span> Price:  500  gp</li></ul>\n</div>   \n<div style=\"clear: both;\"></div></div>\n    <h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Where_to_find\"> Where to find </span></h2>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-tooltip-box\">\n<ul><li>Looted from or pickpocketed off of <a href=\"/wiki/Mirie\" title=\"Mirie\">Mirie</a> in the <a href=\"/wiki/House_of_Grief\" title=\"House of Grief\">House of Grief</a></li></ul>\n</div>  <h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Text\"> Text </span></h2>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-book-text\">\n<p>[A self-help book, purporting to help those suffering from melancholia.]\n</p><p><br>\n</p><p>What of sadness, dear reader, that assails you without rhyme or reason? What if the sunniest of days can become smothered in gloom, with no end in sight? The remedy may seem non-existent, but it is not so. No heart that beats is a stranger to that which gives it joy - you must seek it out however you can. Music can lift moods as easily as flame can melt ice. \n</p><p><br>\n</p><p>[The book continues on at great length, suggesting treatments pioneered by the House of Grief may help, should self-improvement fail.]\n</p>\n</div>    \n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260714202409\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1, no‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.041 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1353/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 18526/4194304 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 5933/4194304 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 29/200\nExpensive parser function count: 2/750\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops 